{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe rain here has been unceasing since Sunday, yet I could not resist the damp. I took a carriage to the Augarten and Nussdorf, where the air was thick but the light strange and beautiful.\n\nI write this by candlelight, and I enclose two small pear blossoms. You will find them odd: the tree’s fruit was already gathered, yet here it is in full bloom again. I do not know how to explain it except to say that life refuses to be contained by a single season. It returns, persistent and strange, much like our own thoughts when we are away from home.\n\nI hope Karl and Immanuel are well. I think of you often in this quiet, wet evening. The journey is tiring, but there is a certain pleasure in these solitary observations. I shall rest now, as the rain does not seem inclined to stop.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080427,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":197,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1135,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-pSoUtW8l6F9wQ25pUCy9e6uEhf6HKe0y","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":922.474,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9834477611940299,"prompt_per_second":1016.8308266682853,"predicted_n":197,"predicted_ms":4669.514,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.824051020408163,"predicted_per_second":41.974389625986774}}